{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6ff8a499-1285-4f80-86a5-8bd2b9a504d0",
    "name": "Piqnex User API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "piqnex-backend (NestJS + Prisma) - the regular, end-user-facing API: signup/login, browsing and posting listings/need requests, contacting sellers, your own profile, and image uploads.\n\nThis used to be one collection together with the admin endpoints (see Piqnex-Admin-API.postman_collection.json for those - split out on 2026-10-03 so the two APIs can be versioned and maintained independently; see each collection's own CHANGELOG for history before and after the split).\n\nQuick start:\n1. Make sure the backend is running (npm run start:dev in piqnex-backend) and Postgres is up.\n2. Import this collection - the baseUrl variable below already points at http://localhost:4000.\n3. Run 'Auth > Sign up' once (edit testEmail/testPassword in the collection variables first if you like) - it automatically saves {{accessToken}}.\n4. Every other request already uses Bearer {{accessToken}} at the collection level, so you can just run them.\n5. Requests that create something (Create listing, Create need request, Create category/brand) automatically save their new id (listingId, needRequestId, categoryId, brandId) for the requests below them that need it.\n\nFor admin-only moderation, user/role management, and catalog management, use the separate Piqnex Admin API collection instead.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
